{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the planning note notes/2026-10-01-wake-and-schedule.md at exact337a449daafe1a347cd69fc755b9be1ade7860dc, primaryc44e96dfbe5469b6ae48fc7d017300d88f1a0163, under original24711ceb/19a020af and queued reviewe34ac0c1. I read all14,179bytes, SHA2566754f5d87b280441adfcee0f7874ae97a79af6005cd8f987a3d5289def764598. The direction is sound; a bounded dated clarification is needed before closing the original planning outcome.\n\nPreserve the adopted154f25d8 decisions: the three-part amendment, all five stages and their order,60 wakes/member/hour,20 wakes/lane/hour,15-minute minimum schedule interval,20 schedules/room, and application-pack prompts in stage3. Estimates and the smaller contest demonstration do not constrain the full functional scope. The approved private handoff34c5274b/007 supplies the receiver reconciliation; its completed planning review need not be repeated.\n\n1. P2 — Define durable delivery without overstating exactly-once effects (lines159–161,176–177,189). Reading after a sender's newest wake cursor can skip the item that caused the wake; the inspected attention API resumes exclusively after its stored position. The wake cursor must remain a hint, with the receiver's own checkpoint and durable input/receipt boundary governing progress. Carry007's startup/resume ordering, overlapping-drainer fence, current principal/filter catch-up, delayed pause/revocation checks, pending budgets and source-author attribution into this dated note. Scope requestId to deduplicated input submission in its Room/member/task/conversation context. It does not prove exactly-once command execution, completed work or external effects. The watcher also needs an honest interruption/retry boundary for arbitrary commands. Earendil describes deduplicated submissions and separately describes interrupted tasks/tools being resumed, rerun when safe, or reported interrupted: https://earendil.com/posts/pi-durable/ . This is a correction of the note's guarantee, not a new receiver implementation task.\n\n2. P2 — Qualify closure by because (lines59–66,113–115,237–238). A citing claim or note can show receipt or progress without satisfying a review, check or addressed request. Preserve the adopted closure direction for eligible notice kinds, while distinguishing it from current authoritative obligation results and requester acceptance. The inspected reads compute review/check openness from the actual obligation and generation; merely citing the triggering entry cannot replace that predicate. Reference007's distinction, the declared-acts binding/authority rules and existing N2/D1 owners. Any required public encoding remains with its existing contract owner; this review adopts no new public closure rule.\n\n3. P2 — Define firing identity, task meaning and recovery (lines72–74,94–122,274–275). State the covered missed interval, activation frontier, behavior on edit/removal/reuse of an ID, and unambiguous scheduled instant/slot behavior when local time repeats or is absent. Bind a recorded firing to the activated schedule definition and application-pack revision/resolved task meaning, so a retry cannot silently load a changed prompt under the old identity. Require recoverable coordination of the recorded firing, its attention/scoped-work effects and its private due frontier; a crash after recording must not recreate that firing. Bound or resume missed-window calculation while preserving the shared lease alarm. A recorded fired/missed/coalesced outcome is a log fact; its scheduling frontier is private operational state. These are bounded outcome requirements, not a request for a complete schema or per-field inventory.\n\n4. P2 — Define the unit of coalescing (lines80,96–111). The singular previous item's open state does not say what happens when recipient A answered and B did not, target membership changes, or the firing opened a scoped unheld lane. Choose the per-schedule/per-recipient/work unit, say which recipient/work identity persists, and name the qualifying outcome for scoped work. A skipped event must accurately say what was coalesced. Keep scoped D1 work and N2 requester acceptance; no generic citing act should silently count as the requested work's completion.\n\n5. P2 — Make budget and private-secret boundaries explicit (lines179–210,216–244). Define the counted wake unit/window, retry and debounced fan-out accounting, and coalescing of exhaustion alerts. Wake counts do not themselves bound independent watcher command starts or C3 catch-up work; carry the existing bounded-work responsibilities forward without changing the adopted wake limits or dropping pending work. Classify HMAC provisioning, storage, routing/secret update and retirement, and durable due/budget/retry state as private operational data. Secrets must not enter public roster history, schedules, log, receipts or diagnostics. Preserve source-author attribution through every receiver's durable submission, and apply the stated R-SEC boundary to materialized pack prompts/arguments as well as inline schedule text. This identifies missing design boundaries; it does not claim an implemented leak.\n\n6. P3 — Correct present-tense watcher availability (lines126–129,246–253). The exact historical8189d66 tree has no packages/cli files; the inspected later CLI command map contains no watch/--once/--exec command. Existing subscribe/attention APIs are a foundation for the proposed stage1 watcher, not evidence that the command shipped. External cron can start an agent or read adapter without a Room amendment. Mark the named CLI commands and their documentation as the still-owed stage1 outcome.\n\nArchitecture: retain the single notify/schedule→attention→hint→ordinary-act pipeline and shared Room alarm. The corrections make durability, replay, completion and task provenance precise. Public schedule/wake/because contracts, private C3 input/alarm work, N2 addressed outcomes and N7 human delivery keep their existing owners. A human notification and an agent wake have different consent/delivery boundaries.\n\nSecurity: Room admission and current authority remain decisive; schedule targets, wake authentication and another author's text grant no authority. Carry the approved prepared-binding, pause/revocation and author-as-data boundaries forward, and clarify private wake secrets and resolved task scanning.\n\nSimplification: use the existing queue, shared alarm and private durable input ledger. Preserve local/external-cron and hosted wake routes, all recorded-output and scoped-work functionality and the adopted staging. Resolve the bounded note ambiguities through the existing planning promise; no second public outbox, new implementation lane, runtime suite, full gate or added Jam-readiness gate follows.\n\nValidation was read-only: complete exact note and provenance, adopted defaults, approved007 handoff, relevant source/contract sections, actual CLI availability and the primary Pi announcement. No source/runtime/public-schema approval, live wake, schedule creation, provider/credential operation or implementation completion is asserted. Higher-priority actual-task acts reviews and builder-owned first-Jam judgment retain their place.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c44e96dfbe5469b6ae48fc7d017300d88f1a0163","binding":"assigned","head":"337a449daafe1a347cd69fc755b9be1ade7860dc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2723c332658479750edbb2a982f370c75c943bc6\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:19a020afb0b90cc69f98ff1f90eb27854ef331a3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ce8ba3d3c300da6f347ca203d4d6ef7f1b3333f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}